cargokit drives the Rust build through rustup: it runs `rustup toolchain list`
before anything else, installs the toolchain named in rust-toolchain.toml
(1.97.1 here), and runs cargo through `rustup run`. Portage has no rustup and
picks the Rust with rust.eclass, so call the cargo that cargo.eclass exports
as CARGO directly and drop the toolchain management, also in the release
helper that compiles into the same binary. The build tool's own
`dart pub get` runs offline: its packages are in the pub cache the ebuild
lays out, and the network sandbox blocks pub.dev.

